Package: Remeans
Title: E-Means Clustering for Large Datasets
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("wook2014", email = "wook20120711@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Enrique", "Toledo", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Original R interface and training implementation"),
    person("Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates", role = "cph",
           comment = "Bundled Faiss source"))
Description: Fits e-means clustering models (Bessa et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2611.09501>). The algorithm uses mini-batches,
    exponential moving averages, and scaling laws for the batch size and
    initial step size. The CPU backend uses 'Rcpp' and the bundled 'Faiss'
    C++ nearest-center search.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/wook2014/Re_means
BugReports: https://github.com/wook2014/Re_means/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: parallel, Rcpp (>= 1.1.0), stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp
SystemRequirements: C++20, OpenMP, BLAS, GNU make, tar, patch
NeedsCompilation: yes
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
